9
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:27.439
from. We'll select Cursor and let Tessle

10
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.519
autoconfigure the MCP integration.

11
00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:32.000
Now when I run cursor, it picks up the

12
00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.079
Tesla MCP server straight away and is

13
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
ready to use.

14
00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:39.520
You've now got Tessle connected as an

15
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.320
MCP server within Cursor. Your next step

16
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.280
is to use the spec registry or Tessle

17
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.280
framework.
